From 706b9b18fefc643216c5014b0cd1a8393649b06e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Niri-RDP rebase <niri-rdp@localhost>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 13:24:53 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 07/12] headless: prepare private session activation before
 autostart

When the headless backend runs in a Niri-RDP broker session
(NIRI_RDP_RUNTIME_DIR is set), niri runs the fixed helper
/usr/lib/niri-rdp/session-autostart --prepare with the configured child
environment before any startup application, so Fcitx5/IBus and the private
D-Bus activation environment are ready first. While it runs, the event loop
keeps dispatching and flushing clients (10 ms steps), so input-method Wayland
roundtrips cannot deadlock startup. The helper is killed after 15 s; failure,
timeout, wait and spawn errors are logged and startup continues.

The wait loop lives in utils::private_startup so it can be tested.

Niri-RDP feature F6. Tests: utils::private_startup::tests.
